Elia understood the loneliness of endless duty. She gathered seeds from every flower in her garden—marigolds, sunflowers, jasmine, lotus—each one holding memories of the Sun's warmth. She planted them in a circle and sang them to life with ancient words.

The flowers bloomed upward, their petals transforming into points of gentle light. They scattered across the darkness the Sun finally allowed herself to create, becoming stars. Each constellation carries the essence of a different flower.

Now the Sun rests each night beneath the horizon, trusting the star-flowers to keep watch. And Elia's garden blooms eternal in the evening sky, teaching us that rest is not abandonment—it is trust.

